# /etc/portage/env/polly-on-env
#
# Polly polyhedral loop optimizer — NO OpenMP parallel codegen.
# Safe for all pure C/C++ 64-bit packages.
#
# Layering: why CFLAGS="${CFLAGS} ..." not CFLAGS="${COMMON_FLAGS} ...":
#   Portage sources env files in order (clang-lto-env first, then this file).
#   If clang-lto-env appended directly to CFLAGS (not to COMMON_FLAGS), then
#   resetting CFLAGS="${COMMON_FLAGS}" here would silently drop those flags
#   (e.g. -flto=thin). Appending to ${CFLAGS} is always safe.
#
# Load vs activate on Gentoo LLVM 20+:
#   /etc/clang/20/gentoo-plugins.cfg (slots 21, 22 likewise) loads
#   LLVMPolly.so via -fpass-plugin and -fplugin on EVERY clang invocation.
#   This registers Polly's option names only — NO optimization passes run.
#   The -mllvm -polly flag in this file is what actually enables Polly's
#   analysis and transformation pipeline. Without it the plugin is idle.
#
# Do NOT use on:
#   - Pure Rust packages (rustc ignores CFLAGS; polly flags are inert but
#     this file is still pointless for them — use clang-lto-env only)
#   - media-libs/mesa (LLVMPolly.so is ELF64; cannot dlopen in 32-bit
#     multilib abi paths inside mesa's build — causes compile failure)
#   - llvm-core/polly itself (obvious)
#
# Flag rationale:
#   -polly-position=early          : run Polly before LLVM reshapes the IR —
#                                    gives Polly the clearest loop structure
#   -polly-vectorizer=stripmine    : Polly-level strip-mine vectorization hint
#                                    to complement LLVM's own vectorizer
#   -polly-tiling=true             : loop tiling for cache locality — the core
#                                    polyhedral benefit
#   -polly-prevect-width=256       : match Raptorlake's AVX2 SIMD width (bits)
#   -polly-invariant-load-hoisting : hoist loop-invariant loads out of loops
#   -polly-loopfusion-greedy       : aggressively fuse adjacent loops for
#                                    better data reuse
#   -polly-run-dce                 : dead-code elimination inside Polly's IR
#   -polly-run-inliner             : additional inlining pass before Polly to
#                                    reveal more SCoPs
#   -polly-ast-use-context         : use ISL context to prove more transforms

CFLAGS="${CFLAGS} -mllvm -polly -mllvm -polly-position=early -mllvm -polly-vectorizer=stripmine -mllvm -polly-tiling=true -mllvm -polly-prevect-width=256 -mllvm -polly-invariant-load-hoisting -mllvm -polly-loopfusion-greedy -mllvm -polly-run-dce -mllvm -polly-run-inliner -mllvm -polly-ast-use-context"
CXXFLAGS="${CXXFLAGS} -mllvm -polly -mllvm -polly-position=early -mllvm -polly-vectorizer=stripmine -mllvm -polly-tiling=true -mllvm -polly-prevect-width=256 -mllvm -polly-invariant-load-hoisting -mllvm -polly-loopfusion-greedy -mllvm -polly-run-dce -mllvm -polly-run-inliner -mllvm -polly-ast-use-context"
